<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pascoal Moreira Cabral</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pascoal Moreira Cabral was a bandeirante from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-paulo">São Paulo</a> who led an expedition into the far west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in the early 18th century. In 1718 his party found gold on the Coxipó river, and in 1719 he founded the mining camp that became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuiaba">Cuiabá</a>. The discovery opened Mato Grosso to Portuguese settlement.</p></div>
